Pipeline for reconstruction
---------------------------
#First execute script to create wd directory with individual folders corresponding to scans from beamtime
script/00createWorkingDirectory

#Run diagnostics of the individual scans to see intensity profile or current correction shift
submitslurm 01scanTimingDiagnostics.sbatch

#Tiff to den format conversion
submitslurm --pipeline-step 1 00tifftoden.sbatch

#Destar of dark fields and zinger removal for flat fields and img produces img/dar/ref_clean.den
submitslurm --pipeline-step 2 -a " --remove-input-files" 02destar.sbatch

#Dark field correction
submitslurm --pipeline-step 3 -a " --remove-input-files" 03darkFieldCorrect.sbatch

#Current correction is skipped in this pipeline but can be run by
#submitslurm 05currentCorrect.sbatch

#Compute extinction by standard pipeline
submitslurm -w wd_specific -a "--remove-input-files --ref ref_clean_darksub.den --img img_clean_darksub.den --out ext.den" 06computeExtinction.sbatch

#This is 180 deg scan, so use appropriate COD detection
submitslurm -a "--ext ext_curcor.den" 07detectRotationCenter180.sbatch
#For 180 scans can be used
#submitslurm -f com -a "--ext ext_curcor.den" 07detectRotationCenter_sinogramConsistency.sbatch

submitslurm -f com 08binExtinctions.sbatch
submitslurm -s  -a "--rotation-axis-file ext_curcor_rotationcenter180.log extb2_curcor/ext_curcor.den" 00reconstructCGLS.sbatch

submitslurm -s -w wd_step -a "--rotation-axis-file ext_curcor_rotationcenter.log extb2_curcor/ext_curcor.den" 00reconstructCGLS.sbatch

#Additional processing which is not part of standard pipeline
submitslurm -f com -n max-ittg001  -a "recb2_cgls_ext_curcor recb2_cgls_ext_curcor_tv -m -0.1" 00TVregularize.sbatch
#/asap3/petra3/gpfs/p07/2025/data/11021463/scratch_cc/kulvait/wd/isit008_5_2_a/recb2_cgls_ext_legacy is very good reconstruction while in excentric cases detection of center of rotation failed
